{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>There shall not be a man's vessel.</b> It is attached [to the preceding] because of going out to war, for a woman was created only to establish offspring, and if she goes out with men to war she will come by the way to harlotry. And likewise 'a man shall not wear' — the meaning is a male whose beard has not yet filled in, who will mingle among the women and commit adultery, he and they, without being known. And this indicates that the custom of Israel was — and likewise in most kingdoms — that the garment of men is not like the garment of women, but rather a distinction between them. And there are those who say [it refers to] [going out] outside the way [i.e., to war]. And there is no need [for this]. Only HaShem abhors one who changes the deed of HaShem."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {0 "The phrase וי״א על חוץ לדרך is cryptic; rendered hyper-literally. It appears to be a secondary interpretation of the war context, but its precise referent is unclear."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:24:20.278805383Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}